#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:79
msgid "The URI Parts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:81
msgid ""
"Once you have a URI instance, you can set or retrieve any of the various "
"parts of the URI. This section will provide details on what those parts "
"are, and how to work with them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:85
msgid "Scheme"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:87
msgid ""
"The scheme is frequently 'http' or 'https', but any scheme is supported, "
"including 'file', 'mailto', etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:92
msgid "Authority"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:94
msgid ""
"Many URIs contain several elements that are collectively known as the "
"'authority'. This includes any user info, the host and the port number. "
"You can retrieve all of these pieces as one single string with the "
"``getAuthority()`` method, or you can manipulate the individual parts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:100
msgid ""
"By default, this will not display the password portion since you wouldn't"
" want to show that to anyone. If you want to show the password, you can "
"use the ``showPassword()`` method. This URI instance will continue to "
"show that password until you turn it off again, so always make sure that "
"you turn it off as soon as you are finished with it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:106
msgid ""
"If you do not want to display the port, pass in ``true`` as the only "
"parameter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:110
msgid ""
"If the current port is the default port for the scheme it will never be "
"displayed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:113
msgid "UserInfo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:115
msgid ""
"The userinfo section is simply the username and password that you might "
"see with an FTP URI. While you can get this as part of the Authority, you"
" can also retrieve it yourself:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:120
msgid ""
"By default, it will not display the password, but you can override that "
"with the ``showPassword()`` method:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:125
msgid "Host"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:127
msgid ""
"The host portion of the URI is typically the domain name of the URL. This"
" can be easily set and retrieved with the ``getHost()`` and ``setHost()``"
" methods:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:133
msgid "Port"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:135
msgid ""
"The port is an integer number between 0 and 65535. Each scheme has a "
"default value associated with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:139
msgid ""
"When using the ``setPort()`` method, the port will be checked that it is "
"within the valid range and assigned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:142
msgid "Path"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:144
msgid ""
"The path is all of the segments within the site itself. As expected, the "
"``getPath()`` and ``setPath()`` methods can be used to manipulate it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:149
msgid ""
"When setting the path it is sanitized to encode any dangerous characters,"
" and remove dot segments for safety."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:152
msgid ""
"Since v4.4.0, the ``SiteURI::getRoutePath()`` method, returns the URI "
"path relative to baseURL, and the ``SiteURI::getPath()`` method always "
"returns the full URI path with leading ``/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:157
msgid "Query"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:159
msgid ""
"The query data can be manipulated through the class using simple string "
"representations."
msgstr ""

