#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:183
msgid "Adding Query Value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:185
msgid ""
"You can add a value to the query variables collection without destroying "
"the existing query variables with the ``addQuery()`` method. The first "
"parameter is the name of the variable, and the second parameter is the "
"value:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:192
msgid "Filtering Query Values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:194
msgid ""
"You can filter the query values returned by passing an options array to "
"the ``getQuery()`` method, with either an *only* or an *except* key:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:199
msgid "This only changes the values returned during this one call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:202
msgid "Changing Query Values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:204
msgid ""
"If you need to modify the URI's query values more permanently, you can "
"use the ``stripQuery()`` and ``keepQuery()`` methods to change the actual"
" object's query variable collection:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:209
msgid ""
"By default ``setQuery()`` and ``setQueryArray()`` methods uses native "
"``parse_str()`` function to prepare data. If you want to use more liberal"
" rules (which allow key names to contain dots), you can use a special "
"method ``useRawQueryString()`` beforehand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:214
msgid "Fragment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:216
msgid ""
"Fragments are the portion at the end of the URL, preceded by the pound-"
"sign (``#``). In HTML URLs these are links to an on-page anchor. Media "
"URI's can make use of them in various other ways."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:223
msgid "URI Segments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:225
msgid "Each section of the path between the slashes is a single segment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:227
msgid ""
"In the case of your site URI, URI Segments mean only the URI path part "
"relative to the baseURL. If your baseURL contains sub folders, the values"
" will be different from the current URI path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:231
msgid ""
"The URI class provides a simple way to determine what the values of the "
"segments are. The segments start at 1 being the furthest left of the "
"path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:236
msgid ""
"You can also set a different default value for a particular segment by "
"using the second parameter of the ``getSegment()`` method. The default is"
" empty string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/uri.rst:240
msgid ""
"You can get the last +1 segment. When you try to get the last +2 or more "
"segment, an exception will be thrown by default. You could prevent "
"throwing exceptions with the ``setSilent()`` method."
msgstr ""

